# inc-g045 phase 4: drives the Learn Spells table for tools/check_learn_table.sh.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/human-priest-mage-dual-seed4-gate.sav \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR=logs/inc-g045-p4 \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/learn-table-check.keys 4
#
# The route reaches the table exactly as tools/keys/spell-tags.keys does: 's'
# for one real turn, 'm' then ESC for the cast menu, 'd' for the character
# sheet and 'L' for Learn Spells. The fixture Kethad is Priest 1 / Mage 1, so
# its table has ONE page, Level 1 (TAB wraps straight back to it).
#
#   t1-table        the fixed level 1 page, before any key is pressed
#   t2-tab          after TAB: still Level 1 -- the only level the fixture has
#   t2-tab2         after a second TAB: Level 1 again (wrap)
#   t3-summary      the box on Enter: At your next full rest / Learn: Endure
#                   Cold (Arcane, L1) / Forget: Protection from Evil
#                   (Arcane, L1), with no table text inside the walls
#   t4-table-back   after ESC: the table again, marks as they were
#   t3-summary-confirm  the same box, drawn again
#   t5-reopened     after the confirming Enter and 'L' again: Endure Cold
#                   reads "Learn at rest", the arcane Protection from Evil
#                   "Forget at rest"
#   t6-sheet        ENTER with no toggle: no box, straight back to the sheet
#
# On the level 1 page the cursor starts on row 0 (Endure Cold, a "[ ]" row).
# The level has no free slot (3 of 3), so the cursor walks DOWN 6 to the
# Memorized "Protection from Evil (Arcane)" row and SPACE unmarks it
# (3 of 3 -> 2 of 3). UP 6 returns to row 0 and SPACE marks Endure Cold.
# Enter draws the summary box, ESC returns to the table, Enter draws it again,
# and the second Enter confirms.
#
# "L" IS PRESSED TWICE at t5. Confirming the box returns to the character
# sheet, but the key the box consumed to confirm is still being unwound, and
# the sheet eats the next token; the second 'L' is what actually opens the
# table. Whichever of the two the sheet takes, the table is on screen when
# t5-reopened is dumped.
#
# The script ENDS at t6-sheet, on purpose, with no System-Menu save. The check
# reads only the dumps above it; a save would add keys whose answer depends on
# the whole flow, and --prove-red's mutation (Enter never draws the box) sends
# the later keys somewhere else entirely. With no @expect behind them, that
# divergence cannot turn the run into a "could not measure": it ends cleanly
# and the T3 assertions are what fail, which is the red result prove-red wants.

s

m
@dump:cast-menu
ESC

d
L
@dump:t1-table
TAB
@dump:t2-tab
TAB
@dump:t2-tab2
DOWN*6
SPACE
UP*6
SPACE
ENTER
@dump:t3-summary
ESC
@dump:t4-table-back
ENTER
@dump:t3-summary-confirm
ENTER
L
L
@dump:t5-reopened
ENTER
@dump:t6-sheet
